  "body": "## What happens\n\n`generate` with no name is documented as regenerating \"every operation that is not current\". After an upstream operation is edited, one call regenerates only that operation; the operations after it **become stale as a result** and are left stale. A second call is needed (the QA run on v0.23.0 needed three). `generate`'s reply lists only what it regenerated, and `verify` then answers `\"skipped\": \"an operation is stale or never generated - regenerate before judging the program\"`.\n\n## Expected\n\nOne `generate` with no name leaves every operation current: it regenerates in program order and includes the operations that went stale because an earlier one changed.\n\n## Repro (MCP, upstream main abe24ff09)\n\nOn the QA project (Face, Island Adaptive, Outside Contour, End Slot, Spot, Peck Drill, Island Chamfer - all ok):\n\n1. `set_operation_area {operation: \"Island Adaptive\", area: {extension: 6}}`\n2. `generate {}` -> `generated: [Island Adaptive]`\n3. `get_job` -> Outside Contour, End Slot, Spot, Peck Drill, Island Chamfer are all **stale**\n4. `generate {}` -> regenerates those five.\n\n(An edit that does not change the stock the later operations see, e.g. Adaptive stepover 3 -> 3.1, does not show it.)\n\nP3: the tool does not do what it says and an agent cannot tell from the reply that work is still stale; workaround: call it until it returns `[]`. Check whether the GUI's Generate All shares the loop.\n\nFound by the QA swarm (SolidCraft v0.44.1 + CamCraft v0.23.0, part p01-flange). Re-checked on upstream main abe24ff09.\n\n**Done means:** after an upstream edit, one `generate` with no name leaves no operation stale (a test asserts every op's status after the single call), and the MCP description matches.\n",
